      "interpretation": [
        "Every relevant verified update contributes to maximum participation and best-update selection before optimistic advancement.",
        "Singleton RPC context is attested-slot fork digest; gossip propagation timing is not an RPC requirement.",
        "Global decoded status summaries may originate from range responses; they are not identity metadata for singleton cached bytes.",
        "Success credit reflects authenticated peer response health, not local durable publication.",
        "drive_rpc_requests internally seeds current headers; guard avoids explicit materialization for unchanged headers, and unchanged transactions skip scheduling entirely."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "Source review and pinned specifications; implementation test evidence recorded separately.",
        "No new memory budget, retention policy, benchmark or remote work."
      ]
    }
  },
  "scope": [
    "Constructed signed objects and temporary state only; no discovery, swarm polling, live peers, remote host or user data.",
    "No benchmark or throughput claim. Necessary verification remains; no-op state/cache/summary avoids snapshot clone and write.",
    "Two baseline participation failures; subsequent cache-ranking failure after removal of stale filters; initial post-fix reopen failure caused by old fixture dates.",
